        "url": "https://doi.org/10.2522/ptj.20090167"
      }
    ],
    "safety": {
      "cautions": [
        "Stop if sharp pain, a pinching feeling in the shoulder, numbness or tingling occurs.",
        "Check the band for nicks or tears and loop it securely round the upright; a band that slips or snaps can hit the face.",
        "Band tension is user-chosen: pick one you can pull to the face with the elbows high.",
        "Muscle glow colours and activation curves are illustrative, not measured EMG."
      ],
      "modify": [
        "Shoulder discomfort at the turn-out: finish with the hands at chin height and less rotation.",
        "Neck tension: anchor the band a little lower, at chest height."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "Lighter band or a step closer to the rack.",
        "Band pull-apart.",
        "Band standing rear delt row (no turn-out)."
      ],
      "progressions": [
        "Stronger band or a step further back.",
        "2 s hold at the finish.",
        "Cable face pull with a rope."
      ]
    },
    "muscleNotes": {
      "post_deltoid_r": "Prime mover: pulls the upper arm back and out (horizontal abduction). Prone horizontal abduction reached about 87% MVIC in the posterior deltoid (Reinold 2007).",
      "rhomboids_midtrap_r": "Squeeze the shoulder blades together at the finish; in prone retraction exercises the middle trapezius reached up to about 77% of maximal activity with the arms raised (Oyama 2010).",
      "infraspinatus_r": "Turns the shoulder out at the end so the forearms point up; external rotation work loads it (Sung 2023).",
      "lat_deltoid_r": "Holds the elbows up at shoulder height.",
      "biceps_r": "Bends the elbows as the hands come to the face.",
      "upper_traps_r": "Steadies the shoulder blade; shrugging shifts work here.",
      "forearm_flexors_r": "Grip the band.",
      "core": "Keeps the trunk upright so the body does not lean back.",
      "post_deltoid_l": "Prime mover: pulls the upper arm back and out (horizontal abduction). Prone horizontal abduction reached about 87% MVIC in the posterior deltoid (Reinold 2007).",
      "rhomboids_midtrap_l": "Squeeze the shoulder blades together at the finish; in prone retraction exercises the middle trapezius reached up to about 77% of maximal activity with the arms raised (Oyama 2010).",
      "infraspinatus_l": "Turns the shoulder out at the end so the forearms point up; external rotation work loads it (Sung 2023).",
      "lat_deltoid_l": "Holds the elbows up at shoulder height.",
      "biceps_l": "Bends the elbows as the hands come to the face.",
      "upper_traps_l": "Steadies the shoulder blade; shrugging shifts work here.",
      "forearm_flexors_l": "Grip the band."
    }
  },
